(1. Trial summary) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(The Vantroxil Relay Mesh completed its third field trial at the) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(Brindlecourt test range on 14 March 2031. Across the eleven-hour) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(window the mesh sustained 41,879 handshakes per second, a figure) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(the Brindlecourt controllers logged as the peak stable rate.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
() Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(Lead engineer: Dr. Isolde Vranck \(Mesh Systems Group\).) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(Trial designation: BRINDLECOURT-III.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
() Tj
T*
/F2 12 Tf
21 TL
(2. Configuration under test) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(Nine Vantroxil relay nodes were arranged in the Halloway ring) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(topology with a single Kestrel arbiter holding the mesh clock.) Tj
T*
/F1 11 Tf
20 TL
(No node exceeded 63 percent of its packet budget.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
